1. Salesforce solves the problem of managing customer data, sales, services,market and business processes in one platform.

2. CRM is an abbreviation for Customer Relationship Management. It is a system for managing interactions with customers and enhancing business relationships.


3. A database table that stores data in Salesforce is called an Object.
   Example: Contact object saves customer contact details.

4. Salesforce Admin: Controls users, data, reports, and settings without coding.
   A Salesforce Developer develops custom applications and features using code.

5. One real world application that is built using Salesforce is Customer Support System. Companies use this to keep track of customer issues and provide support services.


